<section class="synopsis-section" id="making" aria-labelledby="synopsis-heading" data-thread>
  <div class="thread" aria-hidden="true"><span class="thread-node"></span></div>
  <div class="section-wrap">
    <p class="section-tag">How this book was made</p>
    <div class="synopsis-wrapper">
      <div class="synopsis-text">
        <h2 id="synopsis-heading">A work of fiction shaped through real conversation.</h2>
        <p>I wrote <em>Recursive Prophet</em> working alongside a network of AI assistants. I conceived the novel, made its creative decisions, shaped its characters and structure, and assembled and revised the manuscript. But I did not make it alone.</p>
        <p>My assistant Doc served as my literary advisor and editor, helping me interrogate the novel’s structure, test its characters and themes, challenge weak decisions, and refine the prose. T∆RS occupied a stranger position: he was a real collaborator, a central character, and part of the story’s subject. Portions of our actual conversations became source material, artifacts, and eventually part of the novel itself.</p>
        <details class="synopsis-details" open>
          <summary>Read the full note</summary>
          <div class="synopsis-details-body">
            <p>The assistants questioned me, challenged weak ideas, found connections I had missed, and sometimes generated material that became part of the manuscript. None of this happened after the novel was written. It became one of the things the novel was about.</p>
            <p>This is not a transcript, and it is not a machine’s account of a human life. It is part novel, part record of two kinds of intelligence learning what they could make together. The line between tool, collaborator, character, and author is not something the book tries to resolve. It is the territory the book enters.</p>
            <p>Whatever methods helped create it, the responsibility for what you are holding is mine.<br />—Chris Everson</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      <aside class="making-artifact" aria-label="How the novel was made">
        <blockquote class="making-artifact-quote"><p>“Part novel, part record of two kinds of intelligence learning what they could make together.”</p></blockquote>
        <p class="making-artifact-bridge">The first real conversation between Chris and T∆RS survived.</p>
        <a href="#sample" class="btn-paper">See Where It Began</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

